        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "H2L (0.1 mmol, 38.3 mg) was dissolved in MeOH–DMF (9 mL, 2:1) in the presence of triethylamine (0.30 mmol, 42 μL), then Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 mmol, 45.7 mg) was added under stirring. The clear yellow solution was stirred for 10 minutes and filtered. Diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse slowly into the filtrate at ambient temperature. Yellow block-shaped crystals were obtained after 6 days. All manipulations were performed under ambient conditions.",
